-- title:
--   Corner rank of H¹ scales by the index [H':H]
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero level $L$, a set $S$ of natural numbers, and a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}$ of characteristic zero (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal) whose residue field $k$ has characteristic a prime $p$. Let $H \le H'$ be subgroups of $(\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$ with relative index $H.\mathrm{relIndex}\,H' = p^n$ for some $n$, and suppose some divisor $r \mid L$ with $r \ge 4$ is such that every $u \in H'$ reduces to $1$ in $\mathbb{Z}/r$. Let $G$ be a type and $\varphi : G \to \mathtt{Gen}\,L\,S$ a family of formal Hecke symbols — each either $T_\ell$ for a prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$, or $U_q$ for a prime $q \mid L$, or a diamond $\langle d\rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$ — together with $dG : H' \to G$ such that $\varphi(dG\,u) = \langle u\rangle$, so all diamonds of elements of $H'$ occur in the family. Assume the induced operators `opFamily` commute pairwise on $H^1(L,H,\mathcal{O}) = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal{O})$ and on $H^1(L,H',\mathcal{O})$, where $\Gamma_H(L) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ is the preimage of $H$ in $\Gamma_0(L)$. Let $\bar\theta : G \to k$. Let $Sp$ be an `IdempotentSplitting` of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1(L,H,\mathcal{O}))$ generated by the operators $\varphi(g)$, i.e. a finite family of complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals and satisfying $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j \iff i \ne j$; fix an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0} B e_{i_0}$ to $k$ carrying the image of each operator $\varphi(g)$ to $\bar\theta(g)$. Let $Sp'$, $i_0'$, $\pi_{k}'$ be the same data at level $H'$. Assume finally the non-Eisenstein condition: there are $g \in G$ and a prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$, $\varphi(g) = T_\ell$, $\ell \equiv 1 \pmod L$ and $\bar\theta(g) \ne \ell + 1$ in $k$. Then the $\mathcal{O}$-rank of the corner submodule $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1(L,H,\mathcal{O})$ equals $H.\mathrm{relIndex}\,H'$ times the $\mathcal{O}$-rank of $e_{i_0'} \cdot H^1(L,H',\mathcal{O})$.
--
--   This is the numerical form of the Taylor–Wiles freeness statement for weight-two group cohomology localised at a non-Eisenstein maximal ideal: passing from level $\Gamma_{H'}(L)$ to the $p$-power covering $\Gamma_H(L)$ multiplies the rank of the localised cohomology by the index $[H':H]$, here for the Hecke algebra generated by an arbitrary commuting subfamily of operators containing the diamonds of $H'$. It feeds the construction of a basis exhibiting the corner of $H^1(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal{O})$ as free over the group algebra $\mathcal{O}[H'/H]$.
